hadiths[108]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And the goat: if you show mercy to it, Allah will show mercy to you."""
"7056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! There is no believer on earth but that I am the one with the most right to him among all people. So whoever of you leaves behind a debt or helpless dependants, I am responsible for him; and whoever of you leaves behind wealth, it will go to his paternal kin ('asabah), whoever they may be."""
"7057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise, for none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and among the idolaters you are only like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or like a black hair on the hide of a red bull."""
"7058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah and Juhaynah, and whoever is from Muzaynah, are better in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection than Asad, Tayy and Ghatafan."""
"7059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! The handkerchiefs of Sa'd bin Mu'adh in Paradise are finer than this."""
"7060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! A day will surely come upon one of you when seeing me, and then seeing me again, will be dearer to him than his family and his wealth together."""
"7061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! In the morning the family of Muhammad had neither a sa' of grain nor a sa' of dates."""
"7062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! Any servant who believes and then keeps to the right course will be admitted into Paradise. I hope that no one will enter it until you and those of your offspring who are righteous have settled in dwellings in Paradise. And my Lord has promised me that seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning."""
"7063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! Anyone of this Ummah who hears of me, whether Jew or Christian, and then dies without believing in the message with which I have been sent, will be among the people of the Fire."""
"7064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The miscarried child will pull its mother by its umbilical cord into Paradise, provided she sought reward (from Allah) for its loss."""
"7065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The cloak that he took from the spoils on the day of Khaybar, which had not yet been reached by the distribution, is now blazing upon him as fire."""
"7066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The vessels of this Pond are more numerous than the stars and planets of the sky on a dark, clear night. Its vessels are the vessels of Paradise; whoever drinks from it will never feel thirst again. Two channels from Paradise flow into it; whoever drinks from it will not feel thirst. Its width is like its length, from Amman to Aylah. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey."""
"7067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! I will drive some men away from my Pond just as a stray camel is driven away from the watering trough."""
"7068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! I shall judge between you two according to the Book of Allah: the slave-girl and the sheep are to be returned to you, and your son is to receive one hundred lashes and exile for one year, and the wife of this man is to be stoned. O Unays! Go to the wife of this man, and if she confesses, stone her."""
"7069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! For one of you to take his rope and carry firewood on his back is better for him than to go to a man and ask him, whether he gives him or refuses him."""
"7070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You must enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, or else Allah may soon send upon you a punishment from Himself; then you will call upon Him and He will not answer you."""
"7071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You will certainly be asked about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger drove you out of your houses, and you did not return until you had received this blessing."""
"7072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! I had resolved to order that firewood be gathered, then to order the prayer so that the call to prayer (adhan) is given for it, then to order a man to lead the people, and then to go myself to those men and burn their houses down upon them. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If any of them knew that he would find a fat bone or two good hooves, he would certainly attend the Isha prayer."""
"7073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If you remained in your homes in the same state that you are in when you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you and shade you with their wings. But, O Hanzalah, some time is for worship and some time is for worldly affairs."""
"7074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If you did not commit sins, Allah would take you away and bring a people who would commit sins, then seek forgiveness from Allah, and He would forgive them."""
"7075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Were it not that some of the believing men would not be content to stay behind me, and I do not have mounts for them, I would not stay behind any expedition fighting in the path of Allah. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! I would love to be killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed."""
"7076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! A time will surely come upon the people when the killer will not know for what he killed, and the one killed will not know for what he was killed."""
"7077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Soon the son of Maryam will descend among you as a just judge and a fair leader. He will break the cross, kill the swine and abolish the jizyah, and wealth will increase so much that no one will accept it, until a single prostration will be better than the world and everything in it."""
"7078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The son of Maryam will enter the state of ihram at Fajj al-Rawha' for Hajj or Umrah, or he will combine the two."""
"7079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Nothing like it (Umm al-Qur'an, that is, Surah al-Fatihah) was revealed in the Torah, nor in the Injil, nor in the Zabur, nor in the Qur'an. It is the seven oft-repeated verses and the Mighty Qur'an which I have been given."""
"7080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! There is no man who calls his wife to his bed and she refuses him, except that the One Who is in the heaven remains displeased with her until he is pleased with her."""
"7081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not tell you of something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread the greeting of salam among yourselves."""
"7082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The world will not come to an end until a man passes by a grave, rolls over it and says: 'Would that I were in the place of the occupant of this grave!' And it will not be religion that drives him to say this, but only affliction."""
"7083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The Hour will not be established until wild beasts speak to human beings, and until the tip of a man's whip and the strap of his sandal speak to him, and his thigh informs him of what his family did after him."""
"7084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! None of you will be a believer until I am dearer to him than his father and his children."""
"7085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! No servant will be a believer until he loves for his brother the good that he loves for himself."""
"7086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! No servant will be a believer until he loves for his neighbour what he loves for himself."""
"7087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Whoever harms my uncle has harmed me, for a man's paternal uncle is just like his father."""
"7088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Anyone who is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound gushing; its colour will be the colour of blood and its scent the scent of musk."""
"7089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah! You are the best of Allah's lands and the most beloved of Allah's lands to me, and had I not been driven out of you, I would never have left."""
"7090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah! I hope that I am the one among you who fears Allah the most and knows best what to guard against."""
"7091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, I say 'Astaghfirullaha wa atubu ilayh' (I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him in repentance) more than seventy times a day."""
"7092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, I hear the crying of a child while I am in prayer, so I shorten the prayer, fearing that his mother may become distressed."""
"7093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, for one of you to persist in his oath and remain at odds with his family because of it is a greater sin in the sight of Allah than for him to pay the expiation that Allah has made obligatory upon him."""
"7094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, that a single man be guided through you is better for you than red camels."""
"7095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, Allah will not cast His beloved into the Fire."""
"7096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, the world is even more insignificant in the sight of Allah than this thing is insignificant to you."""
"7097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, Allah is more delighted with the repentance of His servant than a man who is travelling in a desolate land; he takes shelter in the shade of a tree and falls asleep beneath it, then wakes up and does not find his mount. He climbs a high place but sees nothing, then climbs another high place and looks, but sees nothing. So he says: 'I will go back to the very place where I was and stay there until I die.' So he goes back, and suddenly there is his mount, dragging its halter. So Allah is more delighted with the repentance of His servant than this man was at finding his mount."""
"7098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, Allah will raise it, that is, the Black Stone, on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it will see and a tongue with which it will speak, and it will bear witness in favour of whoever touched it in truth."""
"7099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, the son of Maryam will certainly descend as a just ruler. He will break the cross, kill the swine and abolish the jizyah; the young she-camels will be left alone and no one will strive after them; enmity, hatred and envy will disappear; and people will be called to take wealth, but no one will accept it."""
"7100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, the world compared to the Hereafter is no more than if one of you were to put this finger of his into the sea, then let him see what it brings back."""
"7101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, after me you will not find anyone more just towards you than me."""
"7102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, he is not a believer! By Allah, he is not a believer! By Allah, he is not a believer! The one whose neighbour is not safe from his harm."""
"7103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, after this day of mine I will not accept a gift from anyone unless he is a Qurashi Muhajir, or one of the Ansar, or from Daws, or from Thaqif."""
"7104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And what disease is more incurable than miserliness?"""
"7105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the two Eids, going out to the place of Eid prayer is obligatory upon every adult woman."""
"7106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has become due. You are witnesses on the earth."""
"7107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your charity has been accepted, and your garden has been returned to you."""
"7108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I wish that I could meet my brothers who believed in me without having seen me."""
"7109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The illness of a believer is an expiation for his sins."""
"7110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accountability has been lifted from my Ummah for mistakes, forgetfulness and what they are forced to do."""
"7111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Lord has promised me that seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment, and with every thousand another seventy thousand, and in addition to that, three handfuls from the handfuls of my Lord."""
"7112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The guests of Allah are three: the one who fights in His cause, the one performing Hajj, and the one performing Umrah."""
"7113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let your beards grow and trim your moustaches."""
"7114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let your beards grow and cut your moustaches."""
"7115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The time of the Zuhr prayer is when the sun has passed its zenith and a man's shadow is equal to his height, as long as the time of Asr has not come. The time of the Asr prayer is as long as the sun has not turned yellow. The time of the Maghrib prayer is as long as the twilight has not disappeared. The time of the Isha prayer is until the middle of the night. And the time of the Fajr prayer is from the breaking of dawn until the sun rises; so when the sun rises, refrain from praying, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."""
"7116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was protected from your evil, and you were protected from its evil."""
"7117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The eyes are what keep the private part closed, so whoever sleeps should perform ablution (wudu)."""
"7118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, all the children of Adam will be under my banner, and I will be the first for whom the gate of Paradise is opened."""
"7119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's children are part of his earnings, indeed the best of his earnings, so eat from their wealth."""
"7120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The child born of fornication is the worst of the three."""
"7121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight a son has been born to me, and I have named him after my father Ibrahim."""
"7122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And why should any of you not do that? For there is no created soul except that Allah is its Creator."""
"7123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What have I to do with the world, and what have I to do with decorative designs?"""
"7124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you consider martyrdom to be only for the one who is killed in the cause of Allah? If that were so, your martyrs would be very few! Being killed in the cause of Allah is martyrdom, dying of a disease of the belly is martyrdom, dying by burning is martyrdom, dying by drowning is martyrdom, dying by being crushed is martyrdom, dying of pleurisy is martyrdom, and the woman who dies while pregnant is also a martyr."""
"7125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How did you know that it is a ruqyah (something to recite over the sick)? You did the right thing. Divide it, and keep a share for me along with yourselves."""
"7126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What do you know? Perhaps Allah has looked at the people of Badr and said: 'Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.'"""
"7127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Has Aqil left us any house?"""
"7128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do camels give birth to anything other than camels?"""
"7129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to Ammar! A rebellious group will kill him; he will be calling them to Paradise and they will be calling him to the Fire."""
"7130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! The matter of emigration (hijrah) is very difficult. Do you have camels for which you pay the zakah? Then keep doing good deeds even from beyond the seas, for Allah will not let any of your deeds go to waste."""
"7131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! Do not become disbelievers after me, striking one another's necks."""
"7132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to the heels from the Fire!"""
"7133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire!"""
"7134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to the backs of the heels from the Fire!"""
"7135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near! Successful is the one who restrains his hand."""
"7136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to the one who speaks and lies in order to make people laugh! Woe to him! Woe to him!"""
"7137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to those who amass much wealth, except the one who spends wealth like this and like this."""
"7138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to women because of the two red things: gold and saffron-dyed clothing."""
"7139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! Am I not the most deserving of the people of the earth that Allah be feared concerning me?"""
"7140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! You have cut your companion's neck. Whoever among you must praise his brother, let him say: 'I consider so-and-so to be such, and Allah is the One who will take account of him, and I do not claim purity for anyone before Allah; I consider him to be such and such,' provided that he knows this about him."""
"7141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Woe to you! Who then would be just if I am not just! I would indeed be failing and at a loss if I were not just."""
"7142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman who buries a child alive and the child buried alive are both in the Fire."""
"7143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman who buries a child alive and the child buried alive are both in the Fire, unless the woman who buried the child lives to see Islam and becomes a Muslim."""
"7144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A lone traveller is a devil, two are also devils, and three are a caravan."""
"7145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The father is the best of the gates of Paradise."""
"7146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The witr prayer is prayed at night."""
"7147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Witr is a duty upon every Muslim: whoever wishes may pray seven rak'ahs of witr, whoever wishes five, whoever wishes three, and whoever wishes may pray one rak'ah of witr; and whoever is overcome (unable) should pray it by gestures."""
"7148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Witr is one rak'ah in the last part of the night."""
"7149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gecko is a harmful creature."""
"7150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (standard) weight is the weight of the people of Makkah, and the (standard) measure is the measure of the people of Madinah."""
"7151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah above which there is no rank, so ask Allah to grant me al-Wasilah."""
"7152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution (wudu) is half of faith."""
"7153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution is broken by eating what has been cooked by fire."""
"7154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution is broken by eating what fire has touched."""
"7155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution is broken by what fire has touched, even if it is only a piece of dried curd."""
"7156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution expiates the sins before it, and then the prayer becomes supererogatory (an additional reward)."""
"7157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wala' (the bond of clientage) is a kinship like the kinship of lineage; it can neither be sold nor given away as a gift."""
"7158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wala' belongs to the one who freed the slave."""
"7159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wala' belongs to the one who paid the price of freedom and who conferred the favour."""
"7160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Children are the fruit of the heart, and they are also a cause of cowardice, miserliness and grief."""
"7161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The child belongs to the (husband who owns the) bed, and for the fornicator there is the stone."""
"7162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A child is part of the father's earnings."""
